# Project Legacy — Platform Build Specification Standard

**Mandatory** for every future Platform Build Specification, sprint, feature, module, engine, and experience.

Full template: `docs/project-legacy/PLATFORM_ENGINEERING_STANDARD.md`  
Manifesto: `docs/PROJECT_LEGACY.md`

## Before writing code — Engineering Execution Requirements (15)

1. Analyze existing architecture
2. Reuse existing components
3. Never duplicate business logic
4. Build reusable, modular components
5. Follow the design system
6. Respect design tokens
7. Preserve responsive layouts
8. Preserve accessibility
9. Preserve backwards compatibility
10. Never introduce breaking changes
11. Never hardcode configurable values
12. Production-ready code only
13. Design for future expansion
14. Separate business logic from presentation
15. Maintainability before complexity

## Required spec sections (19)

1. Executive Vision · 2. Player Emotion · 3. Product Philosophy · 4. Engineering Objectives · 5. Information Architecture · 6. Component Architecture · 7. User Flow · 8. Business Rules · 9. Data Model · 10. API Requirements · 11. UI/UX Requirements · 12. Animation Requirements · 13. Accessibility · 14. Performance Requirements · 15. Platform Integration · 16. Non-Goals · 17. Testing Requirements · 18. Definition of Done · 19. Future Expansion

## Before marking done

Pass **The Apple Test™** (premium interaction quality) and **The SquareBoards Test™** (strengthens Competition, Community, Progression, Identity, Trust, Emotion, or Legacy).

Do not ship isolated features — build connected platform architecture.
